.TH BTRFS_CARE 1 "November 2025" "btrfs_care 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
btrfs_care \- automated scrub/balance maintenance for Btrfs filesystems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B btrfs_care
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBbtrfs_care\fP iterates over every mounted Btrfs filesystem, checks recent
scrub status and kernel warnings, resumes aborted scrubs, and runs a
sequence of incremental balance operations.  It can log activity to a
text or JSON file and ships a test mode that drives the logic against
pre-recorded fixtures.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --no-act
Echo every \(lqbtrfs\(rq command instead of running it.
.TP
.BR --scrub-max-age-days ", " --SMAD " " \fIDAYS\fP
Skip scrubs that completed more recently than \fIDAYS\fP (default 50).
.TP
.BR --log " " \fIPATH\fP
Append parsed kernel events and allocation summaries to \fIPATH\fP.
.TP
.BR --log-format " " \fItext\fP | \fIjson\fP
Control the log format (default \fItext\fP).
.TP
.BR --log-rotate " " \fISIZE\fP
Rotate the log when it exceeds \fISIZE\fP bytes (accepts suffixes such as
\(lq10MiB\(rq, keeps up to four backups).
.TP
.BR --test-debug
Force \fB--no-act\fP, prepend the bundled \fIfakebin/\fP directory to PATH, and
skip root checks so you can exercise the workflow without touching
real disks.
.TP
.BR --balance ", " -B " " \fImode\fP
Select how aggressively to rebalance after a successful scrub. \fImode\fP may be
\fIauto\fP (default), \fIsoft\fP, \fIfull\fP, or \fIno\fP. Auto runs 0/5/10/15 usage
passes only when either metadata or data free space drops below the configured
threshold. Soft always runs 0/5/10/20/30 passes, full runs 0/5/10/.../90, and no
skips balance entirely.
.TP
.BR --auto-balance-threshold ", " --ABT " " \fIPCT\fP
Percentage of free space that triggers \fB--balance auto\fP (default 15%). Values
must be between 0 and 100. Ignored when a non-auto balance mode is selected.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/btrfs_care/fakebin
Helper fixtures used by \fB--test-debug\fP.
.TP
.I /lib/systemd/system/btrfs_care.service
Systemd unit that runs \fBbtrfs_care\fP on demand.
.TP
.I /lib/systemd/system/btrfs_care.timer
Timer unit that can schedule periodic maintenance.
.SH AUTHOR
Andrea C. G. Mennucci.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR btrfs (8)
